{#
  Sourced from the developer's shell rc file. Carries no OTLP configuration and
  no bearer -- the collector endpoint is per-client, so it lives in each
  client's own config file, never in a machine-global variable (see
  `otel::configure_shell_env`). Still written 0600, and the rc file still only
  ever gains a `.` line, so a committed dotfiles repo leaks nothing.

  `sh_quote` is not decoration: values are org-supplied URLs and ids, and an
  apostrophe in one would otherwise close the quote and leave the shell parsing
  the rest as code.
-#}
# Written by `governance-auth`: this binary's own issuer/client id, and the
# gateway URL. Telemetry is configured per client, not here. Mode 0600, and
# sourced from your shell rc file so the rc file itself stays safe to commit.
{% for name, value in exports -%}
export {{ name }}={{ value | sh_quote }}
{% endfor -%}
